{
    "word": "manichaeism",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "7d0001ba-8c87-3b90-9d9b-f16ea3fea2e0",
                "word": "Manichaeism",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "237d941a-6892-314a-941b-c9fcb0ef330f",
                        "entry_id": "7d0001ba-8c87-3b90-9d9b-f16ea3fea2e0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A syncretic, dualistic religion that combines elements of Zoroastrian, Christian, and Gnostic thought, founded by the Iranian prophet Mani in the 3rd century AD."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3e86562f-e27f-3963-870f-a81d3ff19ded",
                        "entry_id": "7d0001ba-8c87-3b90-9d9b-f16ea3fea2e0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A dualistic philosophy dividing the world between good and evil principles, or regarding matter as intrinsically evil and mind as intrinsically good."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "92bcd588-fc17-4a2e-a0b3-a715810e9b5f",
                                "sense_id": "3e86562f-e27f-3963-870f-a81d3ff19ded",
                                "text": "In Manichaeism, as Benny Goodman used to sing, it's “Gotta Be This or That.” One thing or the other will triumph, in this dualistic view, and the winner is supposed to be determined in an apocalyptic struggle involving a world conflagration."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3dca4ea1-25e7-4f85-aa62-a6561ef78b9f",
                        "source_entry_id": "7d0001ba-8c87-3b90-9d9b-f16ea3fea2e0",
                        "source_sense_description": "religion",
                        "target_lang_word": "manicheismus",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a48375a1-3abf-463a-8b52-d6a390dab22f",
                        "source_entry_id": "7d0001ba-8c87-3b90-9d9b-f16ea3fea2e0",
